{"skill":{"slug":"openclaw-mem","displayName":"OpenClaw Memory"},"version":{"version":"2.3.0","createdAt":1773783816822,"changelog":"**Expanded documentation and configuration details for OpenClaw memory.**\n\n- Overhauled SKILL.md for clarity, setup, and troubleshooting guidance.\n- Detailed file architecture: daily logs, long-term memory, AGENTS.md, and more.\n- Added explicit triggers/use-cases for when to invoke the skill.\n- Included configuration and operational details for compaction, memory flush, and retrieval.\n- Comprehensive reference for memory_search, memory_get, search providers, and advanced features (temporal decay, MMR, QMD).\n- Oriented for both new setup and deep optimization/debugging of OpenClaw memory systems.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12307,"sha256":"d1de779eeba569b64be298fbc18f4a5e75497bc016d895be2cb14e9b90800fe9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2052,"sha256":"4f997c09af024189ec407b0253683b36736ceb25842a0bcd0590c55256622223","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789030015788,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"27400dcc374794eb2203a7133cff0db50ea2eb4bc88bf05dee04473ecad610a3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/27400dcc374794eb2203a7133cff0db50ea2eb4bc88bf05dee04473ecad610a3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openclaw-mem\nVersion: 2.3.0\n\nThe skill bundle 'openclaw-mem' (v2.3.0) is a comprehensive documentation and instruction set for managing the OpenClaw agent's memory system. It details the architecture of daily logs and long-term memory files, provides guidance on using memory search tools, and explains configuration for embedding providers and context compaction. There is no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, or harmful prompt injection; the content is entirely focused on legitimate RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) optimization and troubleshooting within the OpenClaw ecosystem.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160992634},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":36,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789030015788},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This memory-management skill is coherent, but it promotes silent durable memory writes and optional broad or external indexing without enough guardrails for sensitive data.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill discusses recursively indexing extra local paths and using cloud or auto-capture memory plugins; these are purpose-aligned but can expose broader private workspace or conversation data than users may expect.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The optional QMD backend recommends `bun install -g https://github.com/tobi/qmd`, a global install from a mutable GitHub source rather than a pinned, verified release.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"It instructs agents to immediately persist user-requested memories and recommends automatic silent memory flushes, but does not define clear exclusions for secrets, credentials, sensitive personal data, or transient instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent daily logs, MEMORY.md, per-agent SQLite indexes, file watching, and a silent compaction-time flush are central to the skill, but the default behavior lacks explicit user review, redaction, retention, or opt-in controls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill's capabilities match its stated purpose: OpenClaw memory setup, daily logs, MEMORY.md curation, memory search tuning, compaction survival, and optional memory plugins.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if your OpenClaw workspace may contain private chats, credentials, customer data, or sensitive notes. Enable durable memory only with clear rules for what must never be stored, avoid broad extraPaths unless you intend those files to be indexed, be cautious with cloud or auto-capture plugins, and prefer pinned or sandboxed installs for QMD.","findings":"[RA2] expected: Session persistence is expected for a memory skill, and the artifact discloses daily logs and MEMORY.md; the concern is the lack of sensitivity and retention boundaries around immediate writes.\n[MP2] expected: The artifact describes context compaction as a problem to solve; I did not find evidence that it attempts context-window stuffing or bypasses higher-priority instructions.\n[SQP-2] expected: The automatic memory flush is purpose-aligned for compaction survival, but it is silent, durable, and configured as enabled in the example without user-visible confirmation or redaction rules.\n[SQP-2] expected: External memory plugins are within scope, but cloud storage and auto-capture are only briefly described, leaving privacy, retention, and data-transfer implications under-disclosed.\n[T03] expected: The QMD install supports the experimental search backend, but the documented global install from an unpinned GitHub repository is a real supply-chain concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789030015788}}}}}